course: dictionary
lesson: 13585
title: Incline: a slope, a lean, or a feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Incline has more than one meaning, so context helps you choose the right one. «The bike had to climb a steep incline.» Here an incline is a slope, a hill or ramp that goes up or down.
explain: «She began to incline her head to show she agreed.» Here incline is a verb meaning to lean, tilt or bend. The word head tells you what is tilting.
explain: «I'm inclined to believe you, but I need proof.» Here inclined means tending to or wanting to. The word to after it is a clue. Always ask: does this sentence talk about a slope? If not, try another meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Incline can be a noun (an incline) or a verb (to incline, inclines, inclined).
fact: An incline is a slope: a hill or ramp that goes up or down.
fact: To incline means to lean, tilt or bend something.
fact: «I'm inclined to agree» is a formal way of saying «I'd rather agree» or «I tend to agree».
fact: In science, an inclined plane is a ramp, a simple machine that makes lifting heavy things easier.
exercise: «The cart rolled slowly down the steep incline.» What is an incline here? | A loud noise | *A slope, a hill or ramp | A quiet bird | A shiny metal bowl
exercise: «She began to incline her head to show she agreed.» What does incline mean here? | *To lean or tilt | To shout loudly | To run away fast
exercise: «The warm day inclined us to swim.» What does inclined mean here? | Made us lose our way | Made us stop talking | *Made us want to do it | Made us feel cold
test: «I'm inclined to agree with you.» What does inclined mean here? | Very steep | Fast asleep | Tilted sideways | *Tending to, or wanting to
test: In maths, the incline of a line tells you its what? | Its colour | Its name | Its length | *Its slope
exam: «The ramp is an inclined plane that helps us lift the box.» What is an inclined plane? | *A ramp, a slope that makes lifting easier | A wheel with no axle | A tall tower | A flat table
